   "title": "Interpretation (LLM reasoning)",
   "text": "The docking result indicates a favorable predicted binding score with a reasonable number of polar contacts formed in the target pocket, consistent with the ligand occupying a druglike binding site. However, the redocking validation is a significant concern: the best-of-modes redocking deviation remains above typical acceptance thresholds and the top-ranked pose deviation is substantially worse, while the enrichment metric for this docking protocol sits at essentially chance level. Taken together, this suggests the docking protocol does not reliably reproduce the known binding mode in this pocket, so the predicted pose and score for the query ligand should not be treated as confidently validated. These findings support only a tentative, low-confidence structural hypothesis and do not establish correct binding geometry, potency, or any claim of biological or therapeutic relevance.\n\n*This paragraph is LLM reasoning over the findings above. It is tagged HYPOTHESIS: it contains no numbers of its own and was itself checked against the claims ledger before publication.*",
